  "claims": [
    {
      "id": "claim_02d84355034b43fda096fc817a4fe7f5",
      "statement": "The answer-evaluation flow is driven entirely by a single submit handler inside app.py main(); there is no separate controller, queue, or background job, and the flow only runs after st.query_params provides a valid integer q id that get_question_by_id resolves to a question.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://app.py#L105-L127",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:752f80b6f9f4d94e1d0bf05cf9d5a720576c245dec8c8df0c1db15f642dcac65:"
        },
        {
          "resource": "repo://app.py#L149-L203",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:d03d651a007839f568607e9449431539143061ce95761c5e58be3612ad355e69:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_b8fa9236496c46d3834e21e218731cff",
      "statement": "Session state is initialized once on first load with answered=False, response_text='', audio_file=None, moderation_warnings=0, and moderation_blocked=False; these keys back every transition in the flow.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://app.py#L97-L103",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:df1403d1ae641d9fe643e4707523c3e495f58c77cef7bda11e37326e28dc5b1a:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_486bf0523c9a40e68a83a6d7ee553b54",
      "statement": "The submit handler short-circuits in a fixed order: a blank (whitespace-only) answer is rejected with st.warning before anything else runs, then a blocked session is rejected with st.error and the handler stops before any moderation check or evaluation.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://app.py#L170-L175",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:9368de60b0393cf5c6a7a6933a5cbb92e17da3d501936282d2dbe99c23e74f08:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_1e1c1e2245da48979f10666f496e0f86",
      "statement": "The moderation gate runs only when MODERATION_ENABLED is true: check_text(user_answer) is called inside st.spinner('Verificando conteúdo...'), and when it is false the handler skips check_text entirely and calls _process_answer directly, so moderation_warnings never increments and no LLM moderation cost is incurred.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://app.py#L177-L203",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:1672a6ebf5eeb3590441da173aa1934ff3a24602c2ef3a369c02bd34dc2b73ba:"
        },
        {
          "resource": "repo://src/config.py#L52-L52",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:f5fdce9ed764032fd9fee906023a6c9ceee4ab8146efd83fd0498cafbabb773d:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_aef7f364950546048128b18644fa852a",
      "statement": "When check_text returns blocked, the handler (not content_filter) increments st.session_state.moderation_warnings and escalates via get_warning_level: 'first' shows a warning, 'second' shows a final-warning warning, and 'blocked' sets st.session_state.moderation_blocked=True with a st.error; on any non-blocked result the handler dispatches to _process_answer.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://app.py#L181-L203",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:18e4727905f17e68bcefabb2f12be1f5f1dea5b9533f7556de3672198c084329:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_cd22c56474c648fbbaa2281b9b468d9d",
      "statement": "moderation_warnings increments by one on every blocked result (first, second, and third alike), while moderation_blocked is set True only on the third block after the count reaches 3 and get_warning_level returns 'blocked'; the first and second blocks leave it False.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://app.py#L181-L199",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:2fa7b03a229ab32b427a80d34d7a1d47dcaa220c357e807060cd87244396f2dc:"
        },
        {
          "resource": "repo://src/content_filter.py#L218-L226",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:136ea5579bf4812c79f044f1bc77d15e70c0d8adad4b399c7af219d3d3b75b6b:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_3d3c5769a5294020bc4ce002f8d49f85",
      "statement": "Once moderation_blocked is True, the blocked-session guard at the top of the handler fires on every subsequent submit for the session, so no further moderation check or evaluation runs; the only reset is a page reload (new Streamlit session), because the handler never resets moderation_blocked itself.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://app.py#L172-L175",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:3ed2da830e377253587446cf15e1fe1c298675a22e6faee643ce851762d58b30:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_32816f9f43ab4aa2967fc5bd81e14d4f",
      "statement": "_process_answer is a nested closure that calls evaluate_answer under st.spinner('O professor está pensando...'), stores the result in st.session_state.response_text, then calls generate_speech under st.spinner('Gerando áudio da resposta...'), stores the temp path in st.session_state.audio_file, sets answered=True, and calls st.rerun().",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://app.py#L151-L168",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:f2b6d697f9a62d8c70f6e63a711c926de76664cde6240f231316314ebec1942e:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_75c75003ff5d4d8aa7a194e02ca29098",
      "statement": "The entire _process_answer body is wrapped in try/except Exception as e: st.error(f'Erro ao processar: {e}'); on exception answered is not set to True, so the page stays on the input branch and the user can resubmit without a retry.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://app.py#L151-L168",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:f2b6d697f9a62d8c70f6e63a711c926de76664cde6240f231316314ebec1942e:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_488dda769a2e4422b14adb91f6f7bcae",
      "statement": "evaluate_answer raises a RuntimeError whose message names both the primary (LITELLM_MODEL) and fallback (OPENROUTER_FALLBACK_MODEL) errors only when both providers fail; that RuntimeError is the total-failure surface caught by _process_answer and surfaced as st.error.",
      "evidence": [
